-- A reader that reaches two same-named section binders at once is an error, and
-- the diagnostic names the candidates by their declaring section. This is §§ 5
-- of the ruled §11.4 fruit pattern; the green half is
-- ok/section-given-fruit.l4.
--
-- The three ways out: hoist `foo` to the title heading if it is one thing;
-- rename one if they are two; or bridge at the call, `g WITH foo IS foo`.

§ toplevel

DECLARE Fruit IS ONE OF Apple, Banana

§§ `1`
    GIVEN foo IS A Fruit

GIVETH A Fruit
r1 MEANS foo

§§ `2`
    GIVEN foo IS A Fruit

GIVETH A Fruit
r2 MEANS foo

§§ `5`

GIVETH A Fruit
r5 MEANS foo
